  "description": "Fifteen of the 29 seats in the Utah State Senate are up for election on November 3, 2026. Republicans currently hold a 22-6 supermajority with one Forward Party member. The election will determine control of the chamber for the 67th Legislature convening in January 2027. Key races include open seats in Districts 5 and 6 due to Republican retirements, and competitive primaries in several districts. The chamber is rated Safe Republican by forecasters.",
